  "_approach": "Soca clap-roll into the drop, on a 32nd grid: bar 1 keeps a lightly broken kick and backbeat clap while a soca snare-line pickup starts late in the bar; bar 2 drops the kick and floor entirely and the snare roll tightens from a swung 16th feel to a full 32nd roll ramping to 127, with the last three 32nds left silent as the gap before the drop. Ref: the soca-engine approach behind ukfunky_soca_engine_01 (Roska \"Squark\", Hard House Banton \"Sirens\"), Afroplug's guide to building soca percussion in layers.",
